  "productionCodeChanged": true,
  "problem": "The preceding oversized-journal rejection prevented normal reconnect recovery, including a checksum-valid durable prefix. A checksum-valid unrepresentable generation also stopped opening after valid records.",
  "fix": "Read a capped Blob slice; replay only validated whole records and stop at unsafe generation. Existing worker opening truncates the rest and flushes while the lease is held, after payload-length checks. Payload is retained; only trusted receipt bits reused; full stream/tree verification still required.",
  "redScope": "Five matrix assertions failed before change. Four blocked recovery; truncated-record case already recovered its prefix but failed whole-file-read observation. Single oversized-prefix case separately failed opening. No native whole-1-GiB allocation attempted.",
  "modelScope": "Reported 1 GiB size with small body; actual 300 KB junk, partial record, checksum-valid unsafe generation, wholly invalid journal; append/reopen and exact cached bytes verified.",
  "nativeScope": "Two actual 300 KB OPFS journal cases, valid prefix plus junk versus entirely invalid bytes. Ordinary reconnect without test repair. Bounded Blob reads below file size, no File whole-body read; zero wire resend for valid prefix, exact original wire count for untrusted journal; final saved 120000-byte file independently hashed.",
